      "detail": "Penhallow House, St Austell. 23rd July 1963.\n\n‘Dear Sir or Madam — I am told you are discreet. I have discovered that a member of my family has done something criminal. On Saturday morning I mean to put the proof into my solicitor’s hands, together with a new will. Until then I should feel easier with someone in the house who is not family.\n\nThe moon orchid my husband sent home in 1938 will flower on Friday night, for the first time in this country. Come on Friday, and you shall see it.\n\nYours faithfully, Hester Penhallow’\n\nWritten in green ink. It reached your office on Friday afternoon."
